# Cross-platform

Do not create sibling paths that differ only by casing. Use portable Node
scripts instead of shell-specific behavior for shared workflows. Avoid
hard-coded home directories, drive letters, path separators, and executable
bit assumptions. Verify new tooling on every operating system the project
claims to support.
